# native/llama/PINNED_COMMIT - E1.I4 (skein-ca2)
#
# The exact commits every `third_party/` submodule that feeds
# `libskein_llama.so` must be checked out at. This file is the single source
# of truth; `tools/ci/check-submodules.sh` compares the working tree against
# it and `native/llama/CMakeLists.txt` re-checks it at configure time.
#
# Format: one record per line, whitespace separated:
#
#     <submodule path>  <40-hex commit>  <upstream tag>
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Keep this file ASCII-only: CMake's
# `file(STRINGS)` splits records at non-ASCII bytes the way strings(1) does,
# which silently turns one comment into two unparsable records.
#
# Bumping a pin means editing this file, moving the submodule, and updating
# native/llama/README.md in one reviewed commit.
#
# --- llama.cpp ---------------------------------------------------------------
# v0.4.1 is both the tag the plan (E1.I4) names AND the exact commit the M0
# Fold binaries were built from - `tools/m0-benchmark/models.yaml`'s
# `binaries:` records `llama_cpp_commit: b29c606e...` for all four
# llama-bench/llama-cli artifacts, and `git rev-parse v0.4.1^{}` on
# ggml-org/llama.cpp resolves to that same object. The app and the device
# measurements therefore share one llama.cpp revision.
third_party/llama.cpp       b29c606e28a01b1bc8c1351026a0fa6e616bf6c4  v0.4.1

# --- Vulkan-Headers ----------------------------------------------------------
# NDK r27c's sysroot ships Vulkan *loader* headers at VK_HEADER_VERSION 275
# (Vulkan 1.3.275, Jan 2024) and no Vulkan-Hpp at all, while
# `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp` includes <vulkan/vulkan.hpp> and uses
# API added well after 1.3.275. Khronos' header-only repo supplies both and is
# pinned here; the *loader* stays the NDK's `libvulkan.so` (nothing is
# downloaded from LunarG, and no Vulkan SDK install is required).
third_party/Vulkan-Headers  8864cdc896bbc2a9b6eb36b3218fc9ef57908d77  vulkan-sdk-1.4.350.0

# --- SPIRV-Headers -----------------------------------------------------------
# `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt` opens with
# `find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG REQUIRED)`. It never links the resulting
# target (the shader pipeline shells out to glslc instead), but the
# find_package is REQUIRED, so the package has to exist. Pinned at the
# matching SDK tag; `native/llama/cmake/SPIRV-Headers/` supplies the config
# file so no `install` step is needed. Same lesson the Fold provisioning hit
# (handoff section 5: "spirv-tools alone was insufficient; CMake also required
# spirv-headers").
third_party/SPIRV-Headers   ad9184e76a66b1001c29db9b0a3e87f646c64de0  vulkan-sdk-1.4.350.0
